      <h1>South Korea Battery Market</h1>
      <p class="muted">Battery Market Intelligence · Data period 2023–2031 (varies by figure) · Last reviewed 2026-09-16</p>

      <div class="box">
        <strong>Market snapshot:</strong> South Korea is one of the world's two lithium-battery superpowers (with
        China). Its "Big Three" — <strong>LG Energy Solution, Samsung SDI and SK On</strong> — together hold roughly
        <strong>25% of the global EV battery market outside China</strong> and have committed about
        <strong>USD 95 billion in gigafactory investments</strong>. The South Korean lithium-ion cell and battery
        market was about <strong>USD 8.67 billion in 2025</strong>, growing ~10.7% annually (Ken Research).
      </div>

      <h2>The Big Three</h2>
      <table>
